12.e:
Banisher of catarrh art thou, of tumours and of hemorrhoids;
 Thou banished Pâkâru and Consumption in a hundred
 forms.

All, Agni, that in thee is bright, pure, cleansed, and meet
 for sacrifice,
 That do we bring unto the Gods.

16.e:
O Dweller on the Mountain, we salute thee with auspicious
 hymn;
 That all, yea, all our people may be healthy and well-satisfied.

17.e:
Purely-Bright, Wonderfully-Bright, Really-Bright,
 All-Luminous,
 Bright, Law's-Protector, Safe-from-Ill;
